{"alignment":[{"from":["d1:REQ-1","d2:REQ-1","d3:REQ-1"],"mergedReq":"REQ-1"},{"from":["d1:REQ-2","d2:REQ-2","d3:REQ-2"],"mergedReq":"REQ-2"},{"from":["d1:REQ-3","d2:REQ-3","d3:REQ-3"],"mergedReq":"REQ-3"},{"from":["d1:REQ-4","d2:REQ-4","d3:REQ-5"],"mergedReq":"REQ-4"},{"from":["d1:REQ-14","d2:REQ-12","d3:REQ-4"],"mergedReq":"REQ-5"},{"from":["d1:REQ-5","d2:REQ-5","d3:REQ-9"],"mergedReq":"REQ-6"},{"from":["d1:REQ-6","d2:REQ-6","d3:REQ-10"],"mergedReq":"REQ-7"},{"from":["d1:REQ-7","d3:REQ-11"],"mergedReq":"REQ-8"},{"from":["d1:REQ-8","d2:REQ-7","d3:REQ-12"],"mergedReq":"REQ-9"},{"from":["d1:REQ-9","d2:REQ-7","d3:REQ-12"],"mergedReq":"REQ-10"},{"from":["d1:REQ-10","d2:REQ-8","d3:REQ-14"],"mergedReq":"REQ-11"},{"from":["d1:REQ-11","d2:REQ-9","d3:REQ-6","d3:REQ-7"],"mergedReq":"REQ-12"},{"from":["d1:REQ-12","d2:REQ-10","d3:REQ-8"],"mergedReq":"REQ-13"},{"from":["d1:REQ-13","d2:REQ-11","d3:REQ-15"],"mergedReq":"REQ-14"},{"from":["d1:REQ-15","d1:REQ-16","d2:REQ-13","d3:REQ-16","d3:REQ-36"],"mergedReq":"REQ-15"},{"from":["d1:REQ-17","d2:REQ-14","d3:REQ-17","d3:REQ-18"],"mergedReq":"REQ-16"},{"from":["d1:REQ-18","d1:REQ-19","d2:REQ-15","d3:REQ-19"],"mergedReq":"REQ-17"},{"from":["d1:REQ-20","d2:REQ-16","d3:REQ-20"],"mergedReq":"REQ-18"},{"from":["d2:REQ-17","d3:REQ-21"],"mergedReq":"REQ-19"},{"from":["d2:REQ-18"],"mergedReq":"REQ-20"},{"from":["d1:REQ-22","d2:REQ-19","d3:REQ-22"],"mergedReq":"REQ-21"},{"from":["d1:REQ-23","d2:REQ-20","d3:REQ-23"],"mergedReq":"REQ-22"},{"from":["d1:REQ-24","d2:REQ-21","d3:REQ-24"],"mergedReq":"REQ-23"},{"from":["d1:REQ-25","d2:REQ-22","d3:REQ-25"],"mergedReq":"REQ-24"},{"from":["d1:REQ-26","d2:REQ-23","d3:REQ-26","d3:REQ-27"],"mergedReq":"REQ-25"},{"from":["d1:REQ-27","d1:REQ-28","d2:REQ-24","d3:REQ-28"],"mergedReq":"REQ-26"},{"from":["d1:REQ-29","d2:REQ-25","d3:REQ-29"],"mergedReq":"REQ-27"},{"from":["d1:REQ-30","d2:REQ-25","d3:REQ-30"],"mergedReq":"REQ-28"},{"from":["d1:REQ-31","d2:REQ-26","d3:REQ-31","d3:REQ-37"],"mergedReq":"REQ-29"},{"from":["d1:REQ-32","d2:REQ-27","d3:REQ-32"],"mergedReq":"REQ-30"},{"from":["d1:REQ-33","d2:REQ-27","d3:REQ-33"],"mergedReq":"REQ-31"},{"from":["d1:REQ-34","d2:REQ-28","d3:REQ-34"],"mergedReq":"REQ-32"},{"from":["d2:REQ-29","d3:REQ-35"],"mergedReq":"REQ-33"},{"from":["d1:REQ-21","d2:REQ-7","d3:REQ-13"],"mergedReq":"REQ-34"}],"conflicts":["Recall-trace rendering timing differs: d1 specifies within 60 seconds after the response is received, while d2 specifies within 60 seconds of the user's request. Both measurements are retained separately as NFR-4 and NFR-5; neither reading is discarded."],"spec":{"assumptions":["The responsive web app supports the latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox.","WCAG 2.1 AA applies to the main flows.","Launch scale is up to 1,000 users and 100,000 records in the first year.","Departure is blocked until every expected route box is scanned and wrong-route boxes are removed or corrected.","Unsent work affected by an offline route change remains available for review and resolution; completed handovers are preserved.","An offline handover completed despite a hold or recall conflict is retained, flagged, and associated with a quality case when synchronized.","Denied or unavailable browser location does not block a handover and is recorded as unavailable.","Live temperature, alert, box-association, and history data are supplied through an existing gateway API or feed.","A signer confirms identity using the sign-in method configured for that account.","Customer portal times use the user's configured account time zone.","Recall responses may leave a remainder unaccounted until later accounting or signed write-off.","Handover signatures and delivery photos are retained for seven years, matching audit-record retention.","A Quality Manager is authorized to sign a write-off.","Refusals are recorded by whole box, with a reason for each refused box.","One configured set of tier limits and allowances applies to all products.","Reports use on-screen date-range filters and CSV export; no custom report builder is included.","Quality-decision escalation and recall notices/reminders are email-only from fixed templates, with no SMS or push.","The customer portal and certificates support English and Arabic, including right-to-left Arabic layout.","The existing logger/gateway data and API/feed are supplied for consumption by the web app."],"nfrs":[{"id":"NFR-1","metric":"All pages render without horizontal scrolling at widths from 320 px through 1920 px; interactive touch targets on narrow viewports are at least 44 by 44 CSS px.","text":"The Meridian web app shall be responsive on phone, tablet, and desktop browsers, with touch-sized controls on narrow screens."},{"id":"NFR-2","metric":"All primary driver and customer flows pass acceptance tests on the latest two released versions of each named browser.","text":"The Meridian web app shall support the latest two browser versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox."},{"id":"NFR-3","metric":"Automated accessibility checks report zero applicable WCAG 2.1 AA violations on main flows and manual keyboard checks pass.","text":"The main web-app flows shall conform to WCAG 2.1 AA."},{"id":"NFR-4","metric":"For responses containing up to 100,000 records, all returned trace entries are displayed or accessible within 60 seconds after the response is received.","text":"The web app shall render the full recall trace returned by the service for the assumed launch scale."},{"id":"NFR-5","metric":"With fixtures representing 1,000 users and 100,000 records, the trace screen displays the complete returned trace within 60 seconds of the user's request.","text":"The web client shall support the assumed first-year product scale and make a requested lot trace available through its screen within the requested time limit."}],"outOfScope":["API-side enforcement of credentials, password-reset token validity/delivery, role and access-scope authorization, and account state; web requirements cover forms, requests, screens, and API response handling.","API-side persistence and enforcement of stock/order/route transitions, hold and recall blocking across warehouses, quarantine, quantity validation/conservation, recall trace completeness and arithmetic, recall closure eligibility, write-off authorization, and duplicate-handover idempotency.","API-side audit creation, tamper detection, immutability, seven-year retention of audit records and handover evidence, and certificate-version persistence.","API-side scheduled and outbound emails, including recall notices and 24-hour reminders, four-hour decision escalation, daily summaries, monthly reports, and monthly report generation; web screens display supplied results/status where specified.","API-side production of recall traces within a time limit; the client timing requirements measure rendering after the response or from the user's request, as specified in separate requirements.","Supplying live temperature readings, alerts, box associations, and history through the existing logger or supplier gateway feed.","Importing or guaranteeing initial database contents; the web app provides opening-lot and stock entry.","Pricing, invoicing and payments; route stop-order optimization; manufacturer purchasing and demand forecasting; automatic driver or customer penalties; stock transfers between warehouses; logger hardware and supplier gateway implementation.","Native iOS or Android applications, app-store distribution, push notifications, and background location. The product is a responsive web app; applicable notices use in-app notices or email, location uses the browser prompt, and the web app may be installable."],"requirements":[{"acceptance":[{"given":"A user is on the sign-in page","id":"AC-REQ-1.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the returned sign-in result or error message","when":"the user submits an email address and password"},{"given":"A user is on the password-reset page","id":"AC-REQ-1.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the returned password-reset confirmation or error message","when":"the user submits an account email address"}],"ears":"The Meridian responsive web app shall provide individual email-and-password sign-in and self-service password reset for driver, staff, and customer areas.","id":"REQ-1","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-1","I-1"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A System Administrator is viewing account management","id":"AC-REQ-2.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays account fields and the returned status or error message","when":"the administrator opens an account or submits account or access changes"},{"given":"A user without the System Administrator role opens account management","id":"AC-REQ-2.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays an access-denied message or the account-management page is not displayed","when":"the page loads"}],"ears":"The Meridian web app shall provide System Administrator screens to create and deactivate accounts and assign roles, staff warehouse access, and customer-organisation access.","id":"REQ-2","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-2","I-1"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Route data contains routes assigned to multiple drivers","id":"AC-REQ-3.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen lists only routes returned or assigned to that driver and displays each route's stops in order","when":"a driver opens today's route list"}],"ears":"When a driver opens today's routes, the Meridian web app shall show only that driver's assigned routes and each route's stops in route order.","id":"REQ-3","op":"ADDED","sources":["ASM-5","ASM-8","Q-2","I-1","I-2"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A route has an expected box that has not been scanned","id":"AC-REQ-4.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows the missing-box status and keeps the departure control unavailable","when":"the driver attempts to complete loading or depart"},{"given":"The driver scans a box assigned to another route","id":"AC-REQ-4.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows a wrong-route warning naming the box and keeps departure blocked","when":"the scan is processed"},{"given":"Every expected box is scanned and no wrong-route box remains","id":"AC-REQ-4.3","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows loading complete and displays an enabled departure control","when":"the driver completes loading"}],"ears":"Before route departure, the Meridian web app shall compare scanned shipper boxes with expected boxes, report missing or wrong-route boxes, and keep departure blocked until all expected boxes are scanned and wrong boxes are removed or corrected.","id":"REQ-4","op":"ADDED","sources":["ASM-8","I-2","I-10"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The route service returns stop statuses and update-time fields","id":"AC-REQ-5.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays each stop's returned status and last-updated time","when":"a dispatcher opens route monitoring"}],"ears":"The Meridian web app shall show dispatchers each route stop's status and last-updated time.","id":"REQ-5","op":"ADDED","sources":["ASM-5","ASM-9","I-9","I-10"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The gateway feed returns temperature, status, and alert data for route boxes","id":"AC-REQ-6.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays each box's current temperature, status, and returned alerts","when":"the driver opens route monitoring"},{"given":"The browser is disconnected and cached temperature data is available","id":"AC-REQ-6.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the cached temperature value and marks it stale","when":"the driver opens box monitoring"}],"ears":"The Meridian web app shall show each route box's latest available temperature, status, and alerts from the supplied gateway data and identify cached temperature data as stale while disconnected.","id":"REQ-6","op":"ADDED","sources":["ASM-12","I-3","I-21","I-42"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A stop includes a scanned box whose returned stock status is On Hold","id":"AC-REQ-7.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays “Do not deliver” and the hold reason and offers no enabled handover control for that box","when":"the driver opens that box's handover controls"},{"given":"A stop includes both On Hold and deliverable boxes","id":"AC-REQ-7.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen permits handover only for deliverable boxes","when":"the driver opens the handover screen"}],"ears":"When scanned stock is On Hold, the Meridian web app shall display “Do not deliver” and the returned hold reason and prevent handover of that box.","id":"REQ-7","op":"ADDED","sources":["ASM-1","ASM-10","I-4","I-11","I-14","I-16"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A driver is online and the service reports a scanned box as Recalled","id":"AC-REQ-8.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays “Do not deliver” and no enabled handover control for that box","when":"the driver opens that box's handover controls"}],"ears":"When online, if a scanned box is reported as Recalled, the Meridian web app shall display “Do not deliver” and prevent handover of that box.","id":"REQ-8","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-3","ASM-10"],"stability":0.6666666666666666},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A box is eligible for handover","id":"AC-REQ-9.1","level":"ui","then":"the handover request contains the receiver, signature, photo, actual completion time, and available location fields","when":"the driver enters the receiver name, captures a signature and photo, and completes handover"}],"ears":"The Meridian web app shall let drivers record an eligible handover with receiver name, signature, delivery photo, actual handover time, and available browser location.","id":"REQ-9","op":"ADDED","sources":["ASM-11","I-5","I-12","Q-4"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Browser location access is denied or unavailable","id":"AC-REQ-10.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the completed handover and a location-unavailable value, and the request records location as unavailable","when":"the driver completes an otherwise eligible handover"}],"ears":"If browser location is denied or unavailable, the Meridian web app shall allow an otherwise eligible handover and record location as unavailable.","id":"REQ-10","op":"ADDED","sources":["ASM-11","I-5","I-12"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A driver is recording a refusal","id":"AC-REQ-11.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays each refused whole box with its reason and offers no partial-box quantity control","when":"the driver selects refused boxes and submits a reason for each"},{"given":"The service returns a refusal and quarantine result","id":"AC-REQ-11.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the returned refusal status and quarantine status for each refused box","when":"the driver opens the completed refusal"}],"ears":"The Meridian web app shall let drivers record full or partial refusal only by whole box and require a reason for each refused box.","id":"REQ-11","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-7","I-6","I-7"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The browser is offline","id":"AC-REQ-12.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows each action in the pending queue and retains its entered values","when":"the driver records loading, handover, or refusal work"},{"given":"Queued work exists and connectivity returns","id":"AC-REQ-12.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows queued work being sent without requiring resubmission, and displays the returned sync status","when":"the web app reconnects"},{"given":"A handover was recorded offline","id":"AC-REQ-12.3","level":"ui","then":"the request contains the original handover time and the same handover identifier as the original request","when":"the web app sends it or retries an interrupted send"}],"ears":"While offline, the Meridian web app shall retain loading, handover, and refusal work locally and automatically send queued work when connectivity returns, preserving the handover's occurrence time and reusing the same handover identifier on retries.","id":"REQ-12","op":"ADDED","sources":["ASM-5","ASM-11","I-7","I-8","I-9","I-14","I-16"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The route returned after reconnection differs and unsent work exists","id":"AC-REQ-13.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen lists route differences and affected boxes requiring review","when":"the driver reconnects and the app reconciles the route"},{"given":"Route differences have unresolved affected boxes","id":"AC-REQ-13.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen blocks continuing and shows the unresolved boxes","when":"the driver attempts to continue route work"},{"given":"A handover was completed offline before the route changed","id":"AC-REQ-13.3","level":"ui","then":"the screen still displays the completed handover and its original time","when":"the new route is synchronized"}],"ears":"When an assigned route changes while a driver is offline, the Meridian web app shall show route differences, require review and resolution of affected unsent work before continuing, and preserve completed offline handovers.","id":"REQ-13","op":"ADDED","sources":["ASM-9","I-8","I-14","I-16"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An offline handover is synchronized and the service returns a hold or recall conflict and quality-case result","id":"AC-REQ-14.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the retained handover, conflict flag, and returned quality-case status","when":"the driver or quality user opens the synchronized record"}],"ears":"When an offline handover conflicts with a hold or recall upon synchronization, the Meridian web app shall retain and flag the handover and display the returned quality-case result.","id":"REQ-14","op":"ADDED","sources":["ASM-10","I-14","I-16","I-41","I-46","I-47"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An excursion review receives temperature history, tier budgets, and a recommendation","id":"AC-REQ-15.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the full history, used and remaining allowance for each tier, and the recommendation","when":"a Quality reviewer opens the affected handling unit"},{"given":"Configured tier limits and allowances are returned for different products","id":"AC-REQ-15.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the same configured tier-limit and allowance values for each product","when":"a user views settings or excursion reviews for those products"}],"ears":"The Meridian web app shall show Quality reviewers the full excursion temperature history, allowance used and remaining for each tier, and the returned recommendation, using the configured tier rules.","id":"REQ-15","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-8","ASM-12","I-21","I-22","I-23"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An excursion is within the first tier above or below the band and has allowance remaining","id":"AC-REQ-16.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the single-person decision controls","when":"an eligible Quality Officer opens the decision form"},{"given":"An excursion is outside the single-person case or has no allowance remaining","id":"AC-REQ-16.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen requires a proposal and separate Quality Manager approval","when":"a Quality Officer opens the decision form"},{"given":"The proposing Quality Officer also has the Quality Manager role","id":"AC-REQ-16.3","level":"ui","then":"the screen does not offer an approval action to that same person","when":"that person attempts to approve the proposal"},{"given":"A proposed decision opposes the displayed recommendation","id":"AC-REQ-16.4","level":"ui","then":"the screen requires both decision participants and a written-justification field","when":"a user prepares the decision"}],"ears":"The Meridian web app shall present a single-person quality-decision flow only for an excursion within the first tier above or below the permitted band with allowance remaining, and otherwise present a Quality Officer proposal and separate approval by a different Quality Manager; written justification is required when a decision opposes the recommendation.","id":"REQ-16","op":"ADDED","sources":["ASM-13","I-24","I-25","I-26","I-27","I-28","I-29","I-30","I-31","I-32","I-33","Q-6"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A user is ready to sign a quality decision","id":"AC-REQ-17.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen requires identity confirmation and a reason before showing the signed-decision status","when":"the user submits the signing form"},{"given":"A decision is returned as signed","id":"AC-REQ-17.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows signed values as read-only, provides a separate superseding-decision action, and offers no edit or delete control","when":"a user opens that decision"},{"given":"The service returns an earlier signed decision and a superseding decision","id":"AC-REQ-17.3","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays both signed decision records and identifies the superseding decision","when":"a reviewer opens decision history"}],"ears":"The Meridian web app shall require identity confirmation using the account's sign-in method and a reason when a user signs a quality decision, and present signed decisions as read-only with a separate superseding-decision action.","id":"REQ-17","op":"ADDED","sources":["ASM-1","ASM-13","I-25","I-33","I-34","I-35"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The service returns a release, rejection, or superseding disposition","id":"AC-REQ-18.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the returned stock, order, and route status and disposition history","when":"a Quality user views the affected stock or handling unit"}],"ears":"When the service returns a quality disposition, the Meridian web app shall show resulting stock, order, and route status and the earlier and current disposition when superseded.","id":"REQ-18","op":"ADDED","sources":["ASM-1","I-34","I-35","I-36"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A user opens destruction entry for rejected stock","id":"AC-REQ-19.1","level":"ui","then":"the request contains destruction date, quantity, and witness fields","when":"the user records destruction"},{"given":"The entered destruction quantity exceeds the displayed rejected quantity","id":"AC-REQ-19.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows a validation error and sends no destruction request","when":"the user submits the entry"}],"ears":"The Meridian web app shall collect destruction date, quantity, and witness for rejected stock and prevent entry of quantity greater than the displayed rejected quantity.","id":"REQ-19","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-36","I-37","I-38","ASM-1"],"stability":0.6666666666666666},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The service returns a decision waiting more than four hours as escalated","id":"AC-REQ-20.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen lists the decision and displays its escalated status","when":"a Quality Manager opens waiting decisions"}],"ears":"The Meridian web app shall identify quality decisions waiting more than four hours as escalated in the Quality Manager's waiting-decisions view.","id":"REQ-20","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-37","I-38","ASM-3","ASM-14"],"stability":0.3333333333333333},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Quality Manager opens recall start","id":"AC-REQ-21.1","level":"ui","then":"the recall request contains those values and the screen displays the returned recall result","when":"the manager enters product, lot numbers, reason, severity, and signature"},{"given":"A Quality Manager closes a recall","id":"AC-REQ-21.2","level":"ui","then":"the close request contains the signature and the screen displays the returned close status or error message","when":"the manager submits the signed close action"},{"given":"A user who is not identified as eligible to manage recalls opens recall management","id":"AC-REQ-21.3","level":"ui","then":"the screen does not display recall start or close actions","when":"recall actions load"}],"ears":"The Meridian web app shall provide a Quality Manager flow to start and close recalls with signed actions, collecting product, one or more lots, reason, and severity for recall start, and display each returned action result.","id":"REQ-21","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-3","Q-6","I-39","I-40","I-41","ASM-4"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A recall trace response contains affected locations and delivery records","id":"AC-REQ-22.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays each returned warehouse, box, route, customer delivery, quantity, delivery date, and receiver","when":"a Quality Manager opens the trace"},{"given":"The service returns trace quantities and the lot's total received quantity","id":"AC-REQ-22.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the returned trace total alongside the received quantity","when":"the user views the trace summary"}],"ears":"The Meridian web app shall display the returned recall trace, including warehouse locations, boxes, routes, customer deliveries, quantities, delivery dates, receivers, and the trace total alongside received quantity when supplied.","id":"REQ-22","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-3","ASM-7","ASM-12","I-41","I-42","I-43"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The service returns an active recall notice for the signed-in customer's organisation","id":"AC-REQ-23.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the recall notice, its returned status, affected deliveries, and a response entry point","when":"the customer opens the portal"}],"ears":"The Meridian web app shall show customer recall notices in the portal, link notices to affected deliveries, and provide a response entry point.","id":"REQ-23","op":"ADDED","sources":["ASM-4","ASM-15","I-41","I-44"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A customer opens a recall response for a delivery","id":"AC-REQ-24.1","level":"ui","then":"the response request contains the entered quantity fields for that delivery","when":"the customer enters on-hand, used or dispensed, and destroyed quantities"},{"given":"The reported quantities total less than the delivered quantity","id":"AC-REQ-24.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen accepts the values and displays the difference as unaccounted quantity","when":"the customer submits the response"},{"given":"The reported quantities exceed the delivered quantity","id":"AC-REQ-24.3","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays a validation error or returned error message and sends no invalid response request","when":"the customer submits the response"}],"ears":"The Meridian web app shall let customers submit per-delivery on-hand, used or dispensed, and destroyed quantities, allow a total below the delivered amount as unaccounted, and reject a total above it.","id":"REQ-24","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-3","I-41","I-45","I-46"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The service returns recall progress and outstanding customers","id":"AC-REQ-25.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the accounted percentage and outstanding-customer list","when":"a Quality Manager opens recall progress"},{"given":"The service returns customer response and reminder statuses","id":"AC-REQ-25.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the returned reminder status","when":"a user opens recall progress"},{"given":"A Quality Manager selects unaccounted quantity for write-off","id":"AC-REQ-25.3","level":"ui","then":"the request contains a signed justification and the screen displays the returned write-off status or refusal message","when":"the manager submits the write-off"},{"given":"A recall has unaccounted quantity without a signed write-off","id":"AC-REQ-25.4","level":"ui","then":"the screen blocks submission and displays the outstanding quantity or returned close error","when":"a Quality Manager attempts to close the recall"}],"ears":"The Meridian web app shall show recall progress as the returned percentage accounted for, identify outstanding customers and reminder status when supplied, and let a Quality Manager submit a signed write-off justification for unaccounted quantity.","id":"REQ-25","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-3","Q-6","ASM-15","I-41","I-46","I-47"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The 